<title>GERMANY: Agiv halts due-diligence in sale to MG.</title>
<headline>Agiv halts due-diligence in sale to MG.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-02-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>German industrial holding company AGIV has decided to halt the due-diligence process associated with the sale of a 49.9 percent stake in the group held by BHF Bank to Metallgesellschaft AG (MG), MG said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>In a statement, MG said that despite AGIV's decision, MG and BHF bank wanted to carry out the AGIV sale and were seeking to find a solution.</p>
</text>
